IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `fwr-common`

-- Fair Work Regulations 2009 (Cth) -- baseline-2026-11: the high income threshold (reg 2.13), the amounts added to a
-- dismissed person's earnings when it is applied (reg 3.05), and the remuneration a person on leave without pay is taken
-- to have received when unfair dismissal compensation is capped (reg 3.06).
--
-- Seat: the employee who has been dismissed, or is weighing a claim, and wants to know whether they are under the high
-- income threshold (and so protected from unfair dismissal, s 382 of the Act), and what goes into the compensation cap.
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 57 (F2026C00996), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/F2009L02356.txt.
-- Not deposited, so inputs: the Australian Statistician's average weekly ordinary time earnings (AWOTE) figures, and
-- the threshold figure for the year (published each year; reg 2.13 gives only the method).

§ `reg 2.13 -- the high income threshold`

-- Reg 2.13(3), Steps 1-3 (and the same steps in (2)): divide this year's AWOTE by last year's; "Round the result to 3
-- decimal places ... If the rounded result is less than 1, the rounded result becomes 1."
GIVEN `the newer AWOTE figure` IS A NUMBER, `the older AWOTE figure` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the reg 2.13 indexation ratio` MEANS
    `the larger of` (`rounded to 3 decimal places` (`the newer AWOTE figure` DIVIDED BY `the older AWOTE figure`)) 1

-- Reg 2.13(3), Step 3: "Multiply the high income threshold for the previous year by the rounded result. If the result
-- is not a multiple of $100, round the result to the nearest multiple of $100. If the result is a multiple of $50,
-- round it up to the next multiple of $100."
@export What is the high income threshold for the year starting this 1 July, worked out from last year's threshold and the earnings index (reg 2.13(3))?
GIVEN `last year's threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc The high income threshold for the previous year (starting 1 July), in dollars
      `AWOTE in effect this 1 July` IS A NUMBER @desc The Australian Statistician's average weekly ordinary time earnings figure in effect on 1 July this year, in dollars
      `AWOTE in effect last 1 July` IS A NUMBER @desc The Australian Statistician's average weekly ordinary time earnings figure in effect on 1 July last year, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is this year's high income threshold` IS
    `rounded to the nearest 100 dollars`
        (`last year's threshold` TIMES (`the reg 2.13 indexation ratio` `AWOTE in effect this 1 July` `AWOTE in effect last 1 July`))

-- Reg 2.13(2): the first threshold (1 July 2009 to 30 June 2010). Steps 1-3: $100 000 times (Feb 2008 AWOTE / May 2007
-- AWOTE), rounded; Steps 4-6: that times (Feb 2009 AWOTE / Feb 2008 AWOTE), rounded.
@export What was the high income threshold for 2009-10, worked out from the three earnings figures (reg 2.13(2))?
GIVEN `AWOTE for February 2008` IS A NUMBER @desc The AWOTE assessment for February 2008 in effect on 1 July 2008, in dollars
      `AWOTE for May 2007` IS A NUMBER @desc The AWOTE assessment for May 2007 in effect on 27 August 2007, in dollars
      `AWOTE for February 2009` IS A NUMBER @desc The AWOTE assessment for February 2009 in effect on 1 July 2009, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What was the 2009-10 high income threshold` IS
    `rounded to the nearest 100 dollars` (`the step 3 amount` TIMES (`the reg 2.13 indexation ratio` `AWOTE for February 2009` `AWOTE for February 2008`))
    WHERE
        `the step 3 amount` MEANS
            `rounded to the nearest 100 dollars` (100000 TIMES (`the reg 2.13 indexation ratio` `AWOTE for February 2008` `AWOTE for May 2007`))

§ `reg 3.05 -- amounts added for the unfair dismissal high income threshold (only if you have been dismissed)`

-- Reg 3.05(2): (3)-(5) apply "if part or all of the person's income at the time of the dismissal is paid as piece rates
-- that are: (a) set by reference to a quantifiable output or task; and (b) not paid as a rate set by reference to a
-- period of time worked."
-- (3): continuously employed and not on leave without full pay in the 12 months before the dismissal: "the total amount
-- of piece rates paid or payable ... in respect of the period of 12 months ending immediately before the dismissal".
-- (4): continuously employed, on leave without full pay at some time in those 12 months: "(a) ... the actual piece
-- rates received" for the days not on leave, plus "(b) ... an amount worked out using the formula" for the leave days.
-- (5): continuously employed for less than 12 months: "the total amount of piece rates worked out using the formula".
-- The formulas in (4)(b) and (5) were images in the Word source and are lost from the deposited text (NOTES.md finding
-- 1), so the amount they give is an input. A person with no qualifying piece rates gets no amount under (3)-(5): 0.
@export What amount of piece rates is counted with my earnings for the unfair dismissal high income threshold (reg 3.05(2)-(5))?
GIVEN `some of my pay was piece rates set by output or task` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, when you were dismissed, some or all of your pay was piece rates set by a quantifiable output or task
      `those piece rates were not a rate for time worked` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether those piece rates were not paid as a rate set by reference to the time you worked
      `I had worked for this employer continuously for the full 12 months before the dismissal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were continuously employed by this employer for the whole 12 months before the dismissal
      `I was on leave without full pay at some time in those 12 months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were on leave without full pay at any time in the 12 months before the dismissal
      `piece rates paid or payable for the 12 months` IS A NUMBER @desc The total piece rates paid or payable to you for the 12 months ending immediately before the dismissal, in dollars
      `piece rates received on the days I was not on leave` IS A NUMBER @desc The piece rates you actually received for the days in those 12 months when you were not on leave without full pay, in dollars
      `the formula amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount worked out with the formula in reg 3.05(4)(b) (for your leave days) or reg 3.05(5) (if you had worked there less than 12 months), in dollars, or 0
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What piece rates are counted` IS
    IF (NOT `the piece rates rule applies`) THEN 0
    ELSE IF (NOT `I had worked for this employer continuously for the full 12 months before the dismissal`)
         THEN `the formula amount`
         ELSE IF `I was on leave without full pay at some time in those 12 months`
              THEN `piece rates received on the days I was not on leave` PLUS `the formula amount`
              ELSE `piece rates paid or payable for the 12 months`
    WHERE
        `the piece rates rule applies` MEANS
                `some of my pay was piece rates set by output or task`
            AND `those piece rates were not a rate for time worked`

-- Reg 3.05(6): "If: (a) the person is entitled to receive, or has received, a benefit in accordance with an agreement
-- between the person and the person's employer; and (b) the benefit is not an entitlement to a payment of money and is
-- not a non-monetary benefit within the meaning of subsection 332(3) of the Act; and (c) the FWC is satisfied ... that:
-- (i) it should consider the benefit ...; and (ii) a reasonable money value of the benefit has not been agreed ...; and
-- (iii) the FWC can estimate a real or notional money value of the benefit; the real or notional money value of the
-- benefit estimated by the FWC is an amount". The FWC's satisfaction is an input, never decided; otherwise 0.
@export What value of a benefit other than money is counted with my earnings for the unfair dismissal high income threshold (reg 3.05(6))?
GIVEN `I received or am entitled to the benefit under an agreement with my employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you received, or are entitled to, the benefit under an agreement between you and your employer
      `the benefit is neither money nor a s 332(3) non-monetary benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the benefit is not a payment of money and not a non-monetary benefit with an agreed money value under s 332(3) of the Act
      `if the FWC is satisfied it should consider the benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Fair Work Commission is satisfied it should consider the benefit
      `no reasonable money value was agreed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and your employer did not agree a reasonable money value for the benefit
      `if the FWC is satisfied it can estimate a value` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Fair Work Commission is satisfied it can estimate a real or notional money value of the benefit
      `the value the FWC estimates` IS A NUMBER @desc The real or notional money value the Fair Work Commission estimates, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What benefit value is counted` IS
    IF      `I received or am entitled to the benefit under an agreement with my employer`
        AND `the benefit is neither money nor a s 332(3) non-monetary benefit`
        AND `if the FWC is satisfied it should consider the benefit`
        AND `no reasonable money value was agreed`
        AND `if the FWC is satisfied it can estimate a value`
    THEN `the value the FWC estimates`
    ELSE 0

-- Act s 382(b)(iii) (with reg 3.05(1)): protected if "the sum of the person's annual rate of earnings, and such other
-- amounts (if any) worked out in relation to the person in accordance with the regulations, is less than the high
-- income threshold." The annual rate of earnings (s 332 of the Act) and the threshold figure are inputs.
@export Are my earnings, with the amounts the regulations add, under the high income threshold for unfair dismissal (s 382(b)(iii), reg 3.05)?
GIVEN `my annual rate of earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc Your annual rate of earnings when dismissed (s 332 of the Act), in dollars
      `piece rates counted` IS A NUMBER @desc The piece rates amount counted under reg 3.05(3)-(5), in dollars, or 0
      `benefit value counted` IS A NUMBER @desc The value of a benefit counted under reg 3.05(6), in dollars, or 0
      `the high income threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc The high income threshold in force when you were dismissed, in dollars
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I under the high income threshold` IF
    (`my annual rate of earnings` PLUS `piece rates counted` PLUS `benefit value counted`) LESS THAN `the high income threshold`

§ `reg 3.06 -- the compensation cap and leave without pay (only if you have been dismissed)`

-- Reg 3.06, for s 392(6)(b) of the Act (the cap is worked from the remuneration received in the 26 weeks before the
-- dismissal): "(a) an employee who was on leave without pay for any part of a period is taken to have received the
-- remuneration that the employee would ordinarily have received during the period of leave ...; and (b) an employee who
-- was on leave without full pay ... is taken to have received the remuneration that the employee would ordinarily have
-- received". So the leave days count at ordinary remuneration, whatever was actually paid for them.
@export How much remuneration am I taken to have received for the compensation cap, counting leave without pay at my ordinary rate (reg 3.06)?
GIVEN `remuneration for the days I was not on leave without full pay` IS A NUMBER @desc The remuneration you received, or were entitled to, for the days of the period (usually the 26 weeks before the dismissal) when you were not on leave without pay or without full pay, in dollars
      `I was on leave without pay or without full pay for part of the period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were on leave without pay, or without full pay, for part of the period
      `what I would ordinarily have received for the leave` IS A NUMBER @desc What you would ordinarily have received for the days of that leave had you not been on it, in dollars
      `what I was actually paid for the leave` IS A NUMBER @desc What you were actually paid for the days of that leave, in dollars (0 for leave without pay)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much remuneration am I taken to have received` IS
    IF `I was on leave without pay or without full pay for part of the period`
    THEN `remuneration for the days I was not on leave without full pay` PLUS `what I would ordinarily have received for the leave`
    ELSE `remuneration for the days I was not on leave without full pay` PLUS `what I was actually paid for the leave`
